<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herman Boerhaave</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1668">1668</a>–<a href="/years/1738">1738</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herman Boerhaave was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> physician, chemist and botanist who taught at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leiden">Leiden</a> University from 1701. He brought students to the bedside and is regarded as a founder of clinical teaching, and his textbooks of medicine and chemistry were used across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Students from many countries came to Leiden to study under him, making it the leading medical school of the early eighteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herman-boerhaave.jpg" alt="Herman Boerhaave" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J. Chapman, artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herman_Boerhaave_by_J_Champan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
